> 1) I understand cockatrices can turn you to stone. I've encountered
> three of these critters, all of which successfully attacked me for
> at least two rounds before I dispatched them. No stoning or even
> hint of stoning. Was I just lucky, or what? Should I get rid of those
> lizard corpses I'm carrying around to guard against cockatrice attacks?

Nope, don't ditch the corpses.  Cockatrices don't always stone you.  In
fact, most of the time they don't (at least, not for me).  But as soon
as you get a "you feel yourself slow down" message, munch one o' those
lizard corpses pronto.  You'll be glad you have them, and they don't
weigh much.  Don't carry around too many...it isn't that frequent.

> 2) I also understand you can wield cockatrice corpses and stone monsters.
> So how does one accomplish this? I'm wearing leather gloves and have
> tried wielding, throwing, and applying the corpse to no avail. BTW,
> I'm playing Nethack 3.1.1 on a Mac and the menu selections don't seem
> to be complete for all the possible actions a character can take. 
> Wielding, throwing, and applying never list the cockatrice corpse as
> one of the objects of the action.

Make sure you have gloves, first of all, and be very careful carrying
around a cockatrice corpse (falling into pits, falling down stairs and
many other things can cause you to stone yourself).  Just (w)ield it as
you would a weapon.  It won't appear on the list of weapons, hit (*) to
get a list of all of your objects and choose it from this list.  If I
use a cockatrice corpse (which I only do very rarely), I usually pick it
up, use it briefly, and then drop it like a hot rock.  Too many horror
stories about ultra-powerful characters snuffing it from carelessness or
bad luck with these babies.

> 3) I found a magic portal in a Bigroom on Dlvl 12, which sent me to a
> level labeled Home 1 having a throne with some honcho sitting on it.
> From the instructions I received, I gathered I had reached the start
> of the Barbarian quest. However, the only direction I could go was down,
> only for three levels, and there was nothing special about any of the
> levels, just easily dispatched trolls and ogres. Did I miss something?
> Are the Home levels the same as the Quest levels? I don't think so, but
> I've never gotten this far before. From other spoilers I've read, I
> thought the Quest levels went up (i.e., you started at the bottom).

The barbarian quest goes down beyond the third level, which is the level
with the double doors and what not.  Toward the back there will be a
secret passage leading to stairs down.  Try reading a scroll of magic
mapping to find the stairs.  Use a pick axe if necessary.  You cannot
win the game without getting the Bell of Opening, and the Heart of
Ahriman comes in handy as well (permanently blessed luckstone, gives you
stealth, can toggle levitation).

> 4) How do you level teleport? I've got teleport and teleport control and
> can pretty much jump around within a level (unless some mysterious force
> stops me). Is it a spell, something you get with more experience, or
> what?

Get confused and read a scroll of teleportation.  Or, step on a level
teleporting trap.  Or #invoke the Orb of Fate.  There might be other
ways, but I can't think of them right now.  Incidentally, quaffing a
cursed potion of gain level causes you to go up one dungeon level, and
as of 3.0j (has it changed?) the Amulet of Yendor did not prevent this
form in inter-level mobility.

